PATCH 198: the FUN_0000_d501 FSG chunk-type DISPATCH-TABLE match (pointer-scaling).

Second latent bug in the mission-scenario parser FUN_0000_d501, exposed once patch 197 fixed the
chunk-header read so the "SHDR" magic finally passes and the typed-chunk loop runs.  Ground-truth
under gdb (FIST_COOP_TICK cascade): with patch 197 the magic read yields "SHDR" and the loop is
entered, but the handler dispatch never fires and d501 spins -- no chunk ever matches, so every
chunk is seek-skipped, TERM is never dispatched, a974 never set, and the loop seeks past EOF forever.

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin, 0xd549): the chunk-type dispatch table at
DGROUP:0xe9e6 is 7 entries of 6 BYTES each -- {typeLo:u16, typeHi:u16, near-handler:u16}.  The asm
matcher `bx=0xe9e6; cx=7; L: ax=[bx]; cmp ax,[0xe976]; jne N; ax=[bx+2]; cmp ax,[0xe978]; je HIT;
N: add bx,6; loop L` compares 16-bit typeLo/typeHi, stride 6, handler at [entry+4] (HIT: ax=[bx+4];
call ax).  Ghidra typed the walker piVar5 as int* (4-byte): *piVar5 reads 4 bytes (0x52444853 for
"SHDR") that can never equal the 2-byte a976 (0x4853); piVar5[1] reads the handler word not typeHi;
piVar5[2] reads into the NEXT entry; and piVar5+3 advances 12 bytes = TWO entries.  Every field and
the stride are mis-scaled -> the match is dead.  Int-typed-table / pointer-scaling artifact.

FIX: rebase the inner match to a WORD-offset walk over DGROUP:0xe9e6, stride 6, comparing 16-bit
typeLo==a976 && typeHi==a978, dispatching the near handler at [off+4].  On a match the asm dispatches
then `jb 0xd565` (seek the remainder only if the handler returns CF=1); ALL seven handlers of this
table provably `clc` before `ret` (SHDR d7b5 / DCBS d7e1 / TERM d7da / PATH d87f / STMP d8e9 / PINF
d8a9 / BINF d8d3, verified in the disassembly), so the jb is never taken -> a match falls straight to
LAB_0000_d57e (no seek), reproduced by `goto LAB_0000_d57e`.  No match -> the for-loop exhausts and
falls through to the existing seek path (asm 0xd565), unchanged.  The rest of the loop (seek, the
a974-terminate close+field-copy, the 6-byte header re-read) is already faithful and kept.

OBSERVED (FIST_CASCADE 3-click BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT from repo root, gdb FIST_COOP_TICK, patches
197+198): the SHDR chunk now MATCHES the dispatch table (table@0xe9e6 e0={4853,5244,h=d7b5} vs chunk
a976=4853 a978=5244) and dispatches its handler FUN_0000_d7b5 -- previously (198 absent) NO chunk
matched and d501 spun with no dispatch.  This is the first time the FSG typed-chunk dispatch fires.
The parse advancing all the way to the BINF map-name chunk (which reads "D32.KLC"/"C32.KLC"/"532.pal"/
"5.SKY" into DGROUP:0x79cd and sets byte[0x7a13]=1) is still gated by a SEPARATE, PRE-EXISTING
downstream blocker: the cooperative timer pump re-enters the uninitialised-geometry mission paint
(e714 -> 459a -> 1eb4 hit-test -> 4aaa -> MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_25d1, a `*(int*)(y*2+0x7c8)` rowtable
host-ptr base-loss / op-0x4c present spin) DURING d7b5's chunk read, so d7b5 does not return and DCBS
..BINF are not reached -- the D32.KLC open is therefore NOT yet observed (documented as the next
frontier).  Behaviour-neutral for the 19 verify flows (d501 is reached only by the ACCEPT mission
cascade -- on no covered menu path) -> verify 19/19, default boot rc=0, mainmenu md5 unchanged.
Sources re_out/fist.c stay pristine.

